  "notes": [
    "The Docs library gains *Code migrations*: how to structure charters",
    "when moving a system from a legacy implementation to a new one. Separate",
    "three truths: what the old system does (legacy source charters, frozen",
    "after discovery), what the migration promises (contract charters,",
    "active until cutover), and how the new system works (target charters,",
    "which survive). Add a small cross-cutting hub, route each change to the",
